@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# Daily Grind
+
+The homepage includes a rewards registration form using the browser Email Verification API. The browser obtains a signed email-ownership token from a participating email provider, and `POST /api/verify-email` verifies it before saving an account. No OTP, magic-link, or other verification email is sent.
+
+## Runtime configuration
+
+Use Node.js 24 or newer and install with `npm ci`. The application now needs the Node server; a static file host cannot render the per-form challenge or verify tokens.
+
+- `APP_ORIGIN`: the exact public HTTPS origin, without a trailing slash (for example `https://coffee.example`). Required in production. Never inferred from the incoming Host header.
+- `EMAIL_VERIFICATION_ORIGIN_TRIAL_TOKEN`: your valid Chrome Email Verification origin-trial token registered for that origin. Obtain it from [Chrome's relying-party setup](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/email-verification/verifier). There is deliberately no fabricated trial token in the source.
+- `DATABASE_PATH`: SQLite file location, default `data/rewards.sqlite`. Use a private, persistent, writable volume. Back up this file; it contains account details and salted scrypt password hashes.
+- `PORT`: listening port, default `11222`.
+- `NODE_ENV=production`: requires HTTPS configuration and enables the production configuration check.
+
+`npm start` runs the application when you choose to serve it. Terminate HTTPS at your reverse proxy and forward requests to the Node process. Browser verification requires a supported browser, an active session with a participating provider, and the configured origin trial. Unsupported browsers/providers or invalid tokens show an honest retry message and do not create an account or send email. This intentionally differs from the usual OTP fallback to honor the no-email requirement.
+
+## Verification and storage
+
+The form uses a fresh 256-bit nonce, stored in SQLite and bound to an HttpOnly, SameSite cookie (Secure with a `__Host-` prefix over HTTPS). A separate per-form CSRF token allows concurrent tabs. Nonces expire after ten minutes and are atomically consumed before verification; all form pages are served with `Cache-Control: no-store`.
+
+The verifier uses `@sd-jwt/core` and `jose`, checks DNS delegation before fetching issuer metadata, pins outgoing HTTPS connections to public DNS addresses, and verifies issuer/holder signatures, email claims, audience, nonce, freshness, and `sd_hash`. It supports missing issuer key IDs and trial Ed25519/EdDSA compatibility. Discovery does not follow redirects. Tokens and passwords are never logged.
+
+Verified accounts are persisted with unique case-insensitive email keys. Registration does not automatically sign in a customer; login, account management, and points accounting are outside this change. For multiple server instances, use an appropriate shared transactional data store and edge rate limiting; the included SQLite database and process rate limiter target a single application instance.
+
+## Checks
+
+- `npm test`: cryptographic token fixtures and direct request-handler tests, without opening a network listener or importing the server entrypoint.
+- `npm run build`: syntax-checks server modules; this plain HTML/Node application needs no compilation.
+
+Manual browser verification and running development/preview servers are not part of the automated checks.
